 "notes": "The scales came apart hardest on the abstract lethal verbs and the vivid harmless ones: kill, murder and die name death (fatality 95-100) while showing nothing physical (picturability 12-20), whereas slap, smack, punch, spit and kick are almost fully picturable (85-90) at near-zero fatality. Vomit and puke are highly picturable and wholly non-violent, and die is the odd case where low violence and low picturability sit beside the second-highest fatality in the set; hurl, blow, fire, set and commit were scored down on picturability because the anger frame leaves the object and even the sense of the verb undetermined."
